checks/working-notes/immigration-detention--2026-10-01-supreme-court-takes-up-bond-hearings.md:333:8. Small items. Taken. October 3 remains only on Buenrostro-Mendez. The quote card's foot says "Opinion in his case." The records list names the rehearing opinions and the dockets as of their dates. The July 10 chronology row states that Commissioner Rodney S. Scott issued the guidance to every Customs and Border Protection component. Due process is only in the closing.
data/sources/immigration-detention/cbp-detention-notice-2025-09-18.html:2982:            <div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--name-body field--type-text-with-summary field--label-hidden field__item"><p>Effectively immediately, applicants for admission encountering the Department of Homeland Security for the first time after failing to lawfully present for inspection at a U.S. port of entry are subject to mandatory detention under INA Section 235. Commissioner Rodney S. Scott issued the guidance to all U.S. Customs and Border Protection (CBP) components on July 10, 2025.</p></div>
