Servs., 511 F.3d 324, 328 (2d Cir. 2007). We “interpret the relevant
words not in a vacuum, but with reference to the statutory context,
structure, history, and purpose.” Abramski v. United States, 573 U.S.
169, 179 (2014) (internal quotation marks and citation omitted); see also
Robinson v. Shell Oil Co., 519 U.S. 337, 341 (1997) (“The plainness or
ambiguity of statutory language is determined by reference to the

